DESCRIPTION:Are you curious about teaching science or mathematics\, or alr
 eady working toward teacher certification? Join current and prospective m
 embers of the CSAM Science Teaching Program for a relaxed fall kickoff.\n
 Meet other students interested in STEM education\, learn about the opport
 unities and support available through the program\, and help shape our ac
 tivities for the coming year. Program benefits include a welcoming commun
 ity of future STEM educators\, paid internship opportunities for students
  in science and mathematics majors\, school-based experiential learning\,
  professional and academic support\, and tuition scholarship assistance w
 ith tuition for eligible science majors accepted into a teacher-certifica
 tion program.\nThe afternoon will include a brief program overview\, an i
 nteractive community-building activity\, refreshments\, and time to conne
 ct with other students. You do not need to have decided that teaching is 
 your career! Students who are simply interested in exploring the possibil
 ity are warmly encouraged to attend.\nPlease RSVP through Engage so that 
 we can plan appropriately. Feel free to bring a friend who might be inter
 ested in STEM teaching.\n\nHosted by: College of Science and Mathematics 
 (CSAM)\n\nAdditional Information can be found at: https://montclair.campu
 slabs.com/engage/event/12752357
