DESCRIPTION:Learn where and how to search for books\, articles\, and more.
  We’ll break down the differences between primary and secondary sources. 
 We'll discuss "credible sources\," both those from scholarly (peer-review
 ed) journals and those from other sources. We'll also discuss\, among oth
 er things\, the differences between our two largest family of databases -
 - ProQuest and EBSCO. We want you to advance your searching skills so tha
 t you learn to have fun searching (a.k.a. researching). A perfect worksho
 p if you’re new to college-level research or you just want to sharpen you
 r skills before your next assignment.\nRegister Here: https://montclair.l
 ibcal.com/event/17454786\n\nHosted by: Sprague Library\n\nOnline Location
 : https://montclair.libcal.com/event/17454786\n\nAdditional Information c
 an be found at: https://montclair.campuslabs.com/engage/event/12600604
