DESCRIPTION:Learn about the early history of Montclair State University on
  a 45-minute walking tour of the south end of campus. The tour will inclu
 de historic photographs of the oldest campus buildings and examples of me
 morabilia. We will discuss student life and interactions with the surroun
 ding Montclair community. Archivist\, Paul Martinez\, will lead the tour.
  We will meet in front of the Kasser Theater at 3:30 pm. Weather permitti
 ng – the tour will be rescheduled in the event of rain. The tour is appro
 ximately half a mile long. Most of the route is accessible. There is an a
 pproximately 260-foot section which is partially-accessible due to a stee
 p grade.\nRegister Here: https://montclair.libcal.com/event/17668454\n\nH
 osted by: Sprague Library\n\nAdditional Information can be found at: http
 s://montclair.campuslabs.com/engage/event/12782986
