DESCRIPTION:In celebration of Archives Month\, University Libraries will h
 ighlight how primary source materials can bring marginalized stories to t
 he center of education\, advocacy\, and community engagement. Dr. Melissa
  Benbow Flowers\, Scholar‑in‑Residence at Sprague Library (2025–2026)\, i
 n collaboration with Bloomfield College\, will host a symposium exploring
  how working‑class histories and undertold stories in New Jersey are rese
 arched\, interpreted\, and shared with the public. The program will bring
  together scholars\, students\, museum professionals\, and public histori
 ans whose work focuses on labor\, domestic work\, immigration\, race\, an
 d community change—particularly as these histories are communicated throu
 gh museums\, historic sites\, archives\, and public‑facing scholarship. R
 egistration is free and open to students\, faculty\, staff\, and members 
 of the public—but limited! Registration closes September 18.\nRegister no
 w for in-person attendance.\n \nYou can also attend virtually!\nHere are 
 the Zoom registration links: \n \nSession 1\, 9:30AM-11AM:Centering Indig
 enous Histories: Roundtable and Discussion https://montclair.zoom.us/meet
 ing/register/mFKcJC2GTymrGXonBJVN0QSession 2\, 11:00AM - 12:00PM:Presenta
 tion: "Unveiled: The Narratives of a Predominantly Black Institution"http
 s://montclair.zoom.us/meeting/register/6u_omu0kQxKlsOolZecQzQLunch Conver
 sation\,  12:15PM-1:30PM:Centering Place and People with the New Jersey B
 lack Heritage Trail https://montclair.zoom.us/meeting/register/OjdkxfUPRa
 acoj3h_1DgRQSession 3: 1:30PM - 3:30PM:Doing the Work of Public History i
 n Museums and Community Organizations: Panel and Breakout Discussion http
 s://montclair.zoom.us/meeting/register/pLTOaJakSGu3FCq8kgxCFw \n \n\nHost
 ed by: Sprague Library\n\nAdditional Information can be found at: https:/
 /montclair.campuslabs.com/engage/event/12588981
DTEND:20261001T190000Z
DTSTAMP:20260919T042233Z
